export default "import { Meta } from '@storybook/addon-docs/blocks';\n\n<Meta title=\"Docs/Storybook Architecture & Deployment Summary\" />\n\n# Storybook Architecture & Deployment Summary\n\n## Overview\nThis document summarizes the Storybook architecture changes and deployment process to SiteGround for the Raibach Design System Lifecycle Management project.\n\n## Architecture Changes\n\n### 1. Module Hierarchy Restructuring\n**Original Structure:**\n- `AI Workspace/Column Modules/Left Column Module/Parts`\n- `AI Workspace/Column Modules/Right Column Module/Parts`\n- `AI Workspace/Column Modules/Third Column Module/Parts`\n\n**New Structure (Featured Modules):**\n- `AI Workspace/Featured Modules/Left Column`\n- `AI Workspace/Featured Modules/Right Column`\n- `AI Workspace/Column Modules/Third Column Module/Parts` (unchanged)\n\n### 2. Story Files Updated\nThe following story files were modified to reflect the new architecture:\n\n1. **`frontend/src/storybook/modules/ProgramColumns/LeftColumn.module.stories.tsx`**\n   - Changed title from `AI Workspace/Column Modules/Left Column Module/Parts` to `AI Workspace/Featured Modules/Left Column`\n   - Contains stories: `TopModule`, `CoreBuilderPart`, `ContextAwareOutputAreas`\n\n2. **`frontend/src/storybook/modules/ProgramColumns/RightColumn.module.stories.tsx`**\n   - Changed title from `AI Workspace/Column Modules/Right Column Module/Parts` to `AI Workspace/Featured Modules/Right Column`\n   - Contains stories: `TopModule`, `EmptyTracePart`, `ContextAwareResponseBlocks`\n\n3. **`frontend/src/storybook/modules/ProgramColumns/ThirdColumn.module.stories.tsx`**\n   - Title remains: `AI Workspace/Column Modules/Third Column Module/Parts`\n   - Contains stories: `TopModule`, `ResponseCardPart`, `ContextAwareStructuredResponses`\n\n### 3. Context-Aware Stories Added\nEach module now includes context-aware stories that demonstrate:\n- **Text-level replacement**: Labels and output areas as text outputs\n- **Component-level replacement**: Structured response blocks as pre-structured content\n- **Button-level replacement**: Action buttons with customizable text\n\nThese stories use Storybook's `args` system to allow dynamic content replacement, simulating how an AI system could contextually replace parts of the UI.\n\n## Deployment Process\n\n### 1. Build Process\n```bash\ncd frontend\nnpm run build-storybook\n```\n- Builds static Storybook files to `frontend/storybook-static/`\n- Includes all assets, JavaScript bundles, and metadata files\n\n### 2. FTP Deployment to SiteGround\n**Target Location:** `/prompt-portal-prod.raibach.net/public_html/storybook/`\n\n**Deployment Steps:**\n1. Connect to FTP server: `ftp.raibach.net`\n2. Clear existing `storybook` directory\n3. Upload all files from `storybook-static/`\n4. Set appropriate permissions (644 for files, 755 for directories)\n\n### 3. Live URLs\n- **Main Storybook:** `https://prompt-portal-prod.raibach.net/storybook/index.html`\n- **Left Column Featured Module:** `https://prompt-portal-prod.raibach.net/storybook/index.html?path=/story/ai-workspace-featured-modules-left-column--top-module`\n- **Right Column Featured Module:** `https://prompt-portal-prod.raibach.net/storybook/index.html?path=/story/ai-workspace-featured-modules-right-column--top-module`\n- **Context-Aware Stories:** Use the story IDs from the sidebar\n\n## Issues Encountered and Solutions\n\n### 1. Storybook Metadata Access (403 Errors)\n**Problem:** `index.json` and `project.json` returned 403 Forbidden errors\n**Root Cause:** SiteGround security settings blocking `.json` files in certain directories\n**Solution:** \n- Verified files were uploaded correctly\n- Confirmed direct story URLs work (HTTP 200)\n- The 403 errors don't prevent Storybook from functioning, only affect some metadata endpoints\n\n### 2. Cache Issues\n**Problem:** Browser caching preventing users from seeing updates\n**Solution:**\n- Use cache-busting query parameters: `?cb=timestamp`\n- Direct story URLs bypass some caching layers\n- Hard refresh (Cmd+Shift+R) recommended\n\n### 3. Permission Issues\n**Problem:** File permissions preventing proper access\n**Solution:** Applied `chmod 644` to all files and `chmod 755` to all directories via FTP\n\n## Verification Steps\n\n1. **Build Verification:**\n   - Storybook builds successfully without errors\n   - All module stories appear in build output\n\n2. **Deployment Verification:**\n   - FTP upload completes with all files transferred\n   - Direct story URLs return HTTP 200\n   - Main index.html loads successfully\n\n3. **Content Verification:**\n   - New \"Featured Modules\" appear in Storybook sidebar\n   - Context-aware stories show interactive controls\n   - All components render correctly\n\n## Architecture Benefits\n\n1. **Clear Organization:** Featured modules are prominently displayed\n2. **Context-Aware Design:** Stories demonstrate AI-replaceable components\n3. **Scalable Structure:** Easy to add more featured modules\n4. **Deployment Automation:** Scripted FTP deployment ensures consistency\n\n## Future Improvements\n\n1. **Automated Deployment Pipeline:** Integrate with GitHub Actions\n2. **CDN Integration:** Serve Storybook assets from CDN for better performance\n3. **Versioning:** Add version tags to Storybook deployments\n4. **Accessibility Testing:** Integrate Storybook accessibility addons\n\n## Conclusion\nThe Storybook architecture has been successfully restructured to feature Left and Right columns as prominent modules, with context-aware stories demonstrating AI-driven content replacement. The deployment to SiteGround is functional, with all stories accessible via direct URLs. While some metadata endpoints return 403 errors due to server security settings, the core Storybook functionality works correctly."